Chapter: BoundedFixedExceeded
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 Cost Model, the fixed rung, the arm that must be REFUSED, and it is the
 control for `codex/test/apps/bounded-budgeted-accepted`, whose `digits`
 declares THIS BODY one rung up and is accepted.

 `integer-to-text` reads `budgeted`: its allocation is bounded by a constant
 nobody states, and the digits of `n` decide it. That keeps a `budgeted`
 promise and breaks a `fixed` one. Nothing else separates the two rungs, so
 if this arm ever compiles, the strict flag on the overbudget walk has
 stopped doing its only job.

Section: A Bound Nobody States

  bounded fixed digits : Integer -> Text
  digits (n) = integer-to-text n

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni (digits 4096)
  end
